foreVars[k]}`).join(\"   •   \");\r\n+    }\r\n+\r\n+    return this.formatRelevantVariablesNow(step);\r\n+  }\r\n+\r\n+  buildTeachingSubsteps(step, prevStep, nextStep, bestSubarrayInfo) {\r\n+    const n = step.stepIndex;\r\n+    const op = step.operationDetail || {};\r\n+    const cond = step.condition;\r\n+    const nextSentence = this.buildFriendlyWhatNext(step, nextStep);\r\n+    const varsBefore = this.formatSubstepVars(step, true);\r\n+    const varsAfter = this.formatSubstepVars(step, false);\r\n+    const beforeVarsMap = step.beforeVars || {};\r\n+    const exprFrames = step.exprFrames || [];\r\n+\r\n+    const substeps = [];\r\n+\r\n+    // Helper to push a substep\r\n+    const addSubstep = (data) => {\r\n+      substeps.push({\r\n+        substepIndex: substeps.length + 1,\r\n+        totalSubsteps: 0, // will be populated at the end\r\n+        substepLabel: data.substepLabel || \"\",\r\n+        title: `Step ${n}: ${data.substepLabel || data.title}`,\r\n+        codeSnippet: data.codeSnippet || step.codeText,\r\n+        whatIsHappening: data.whatIsHappening || \"\",\r\n+        symbolsMeaning: data.symbolsMeaning || this.explainSymbolsInLine(data.codeSnippet || step.codeText),\r\n+        currentValues: data.currentValues || varsBefore,\r\n\n"}
{"step_index":1196,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-25T14:02:12Z","input_tokens":3248,"cache_read_tokens":154771,"output_tokens":1891,"content":"### Phase 2 Implementation Summary: Improve Teaching\n\n**Phase 2 — Improve teaching** has been implemented. The visualizer breaks down operations into micro-teaching steps with clear English explanations, shows calculations and comparisons using actual runtime values, explains condition branches and loop cycles, and keeps all substeps synchronized with the execution engine.\n\n---\n\n### Files Changed\n\n1. [app_build/explainer.js](file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/code-flow-visualizer/app_build/explainer.js)\n   - **`AUG_ASSIGN`**: Added support for both indexed (e.g., `c += nums[i]`) and non-indexed compound operations (e.g., `x += 1`, `count += val`), showing operands, step-by-step arithmetic (`0 + (-2) = -2`), and memory updates.\n   - **`CONDITION`**: Added the complete 5-substep sequence to general conditional statements (Read operands with actual values $\\rightarrow$ Compare operands $\\rightarrow$ Boolean result $\\rightarrow$ Branch execution $\\rightarrow$ Reason program moves to next line).\n   - **`ASSIGN`**: Added dedicated teaching substeps for list mutating methods (`.append()`, `.pop()`, `.extend()`, etc.) and arithmetic formula evaluations (e.g., `(left + right) // 2` with real values), explicitly distinguishing variable creation from variable updating.\n   - **`LOOP_ITER` & `LOOP_END`**: Added support for `while` loops (`while_check`), showing condition operand lookups, comparison evaluations to `True`, loop pass numbers, and the reason Python jumps back to test the condition. For `LOOP_END`, distinguishes while loop condition termination (`False`) from `for` loop sequence exhaustion.\n   - **`CLASS_DEF` & `RETURN`**: Dynamic class blueprint extraction (no hardcoded class names) and generalized return statement evaluation with caller handoff explanations, preserving Kadane subarray summaries specifically for subarray problems.\n\n2. [app_build/app.js](file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/code-flow-visualizer/app_build/app.js)\n   - **`renderVisualConditionGate`**: Updated to support while loop condition gates and general conditional statements with dynamic operator badges, operand cards, and branch outcomes without defaulting to Kadane labels.\n   - **`renderVisualCalcStage`**: Updated to support formula evaluations with variable substitution (`(0 + 6) // 2 = 3`) and dynamic augmented assignment operators (`+=`, `-=`, `*=`, etc.).\n\n---\n\n### Key Capabilities Added\n\n| Feature | How It Works in Phase 2 | Example in App |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Micro-Operation Teaching** | Breaks single execution lines into discrete, digestible concepts. | `c += nums[i]` teaches reading `c`, evaluating `i`, looking up `nums[i]`, calculating the sum, and storing the result. |\n| **The 3 Teaching Questions** | Every single substep answers: **What is happening?**, **Why is this operation necessary?**, and **What happens next?** | Displayed in dedicated cards with typography and syntax highlights. |\n| **Real-Value Calculations** | Formulas replace variable names with their actual numbers in memory before showing the calculated result. | `(left + right) // 2` shows `(0 + 6) // 2 = 3`. `c += nums[i]` shows `0 + (-2) = -2`. |\n| **Condition Decisions** | Displays operand cards, operator badges, True/False outcomes, executing branches, and skipped branches. | `0 >= -2` evaluates to `True`, highlighting `ans = c` as executing and showing why Python moves to the next line. |\n| **Loops & Iteration Cycles** | Explains the iteration count, loop variable binding, list element lookup, and what causes the next iteration. | Shows `Loop pass 1 of 9`, binds `i = 0`, looks up `nums[0] = -2`, and explains that finishing the block advances the loop. |\n| **Variable Lifecycle** | Distinguishes creating a variable for the first time from re-assigning an existing variable. | Labels display `Create variable c = 0` vs `Update existing variable ans = 0 (was -2)`. |\n| **Function Returns** | Inspects return expressions, shows actual return values, and explains stack frame teardown. | `return ans (6)` explains return value delivery and scope destruction. |\n| **100% Real-Time Sync** | Moving forward or backward updates the line highlight, variable inspector, memory heap, and substep cards in lockstep. | Stepping backward via **Previous Step** restores the previous runtime snapshot. |\n\n---\n\n### Verification & Automated Test Results\n\nThe suite was verified using automated Node.js execution against all 5 preset inputs and additional algorithms:\n\n```text\n[PASS] Mixed Array (Original Kadane): expected 6, got 6, total steps: 54\n[PASS] All-Negative Array (Kadane):   expected -1, got -1, total steps: 39\n[PASS] All-Positive Array (Kadane):   expected 15, got 15, total steps: 36\n[PASS] Single Negative (Kadane):       expected -7, got -7, total steps: 17\n[PASS] Single Positive (Kadane):       expected 42, got 42, total steps: 16\n[PASS] Binary Search (While Loop):    expected 3, got 3\n       While Loop Iteration Substeps:  3 (Operands -> True Test -> Loop Pass Initiation)\n       Formula Substeps (mid calc):   3 (Evaluate Operands -> Calculate (0+6)//2=3 -> Create mid)\n[PASS] Stack Class (OOP & Mutation):  expected stdout 20, got 20\n       Class Definition Substeps:     2 (What is a class? -> Register Stack class)\n\n>>> ALL TESTS PASSED SUCCESSFULLY! 100% VERIFIED. <<<\n```\n\n---\n\n### Remaining Limitations\n\n- **Animations (Phase 3)**: Variable boxes currently show state changes with updated badges and arrows; smooth CSS transitions and number-glide animations will be added in **Phase 3 — Add meaningful animations**.\n- **Interactive Prediction (Phase 4)**: The teaching area presents answers step-by-step; optional learner prediction prompts (e.g., \"What will `c` become?\") will be implemented in **Phase 4**.","thinking":"Reviewing the requirements to ensure the output explains operations simply, showing calculations with variable values, conditions with operand/result pairs, and loop/function behavior. This aims for clear, step-by-step explanations of the process as it unfolds.\n\n\n"}
